{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שבעה שבועות תספר לך", :translit "sheva shavu'ot tispof lakh", :gloss "seven weeks you shall count for yourself"} {:he "ב' ספירות", :translit "beit s'firot", :gloss "two countings"} {:he "מצוה לממני יומי", :translit "mitzvah limneni yomai", :gloss "a mitzvah to count days"} {:he "מצוה לממני שבועי", :translit "mitzvah limneni shavu'ai", :gloss "a mitzvah to count weeks"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Dual verbal forms תספור and שבעה שבועות signal two separate counting obligations"}], :frame {:text "Menahot 66a records a dispute between Rabbi Eliezer and the Sages: Rabbi Eliezer holds that counting days and counting weeks are not both required (he reads the two verbs as alternatives), while the Sages hold there is a mitzvah to count days and a mitzvah to count weeks. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the doubled language in Deuteronomy 16:9 as support for the Sages' position.", :sources ["Menahot 66a" "Deuteronomy 16:9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מהחל", :translit "meheil", :gloss "from the beginning"} {:he "ב' דין", :translit "beit din", :gloss "two readings"} {:he "מהחל התרומה", :translit "meheil ha-terumah", :gloss "from the beginning of the terumah"} {:he "העומר", :translit "ha-omer", :gloss "the omer"} {:he "ראשית למנחות", :translit "reshit l'minhot", :gloss "first of meal-offerings"} {:he "תרומה", :translit "terumah", :gloss "terumah"} {:he "ראשית", :translit "reshit", :gloss "first"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reads מהחל as 'me-heil' = 'from the beginning of', linking the omer offering to the concept of ראשית"}], :frame {:text "The omer offering is described in Leviticus 23:10–14 as the first cutting of the harvest, brought on the second day of Pesah. Numbers 18:12 designates terumah with the term ראשית, and Numbers 15:17–21 requires a חלה portion from dough as a first-fruit gift to the priest. The midrashic tradition identifies the omer, which is explicitly called ראשית קצירכם in Leviticus 23:10, as the agricultural archetype of ראשית that parallels terumah and hallah as first-portion offerings to the priesthood.", :sources ["Leviticus 23:10–14" "Leviticus 23:10" "Numbers 18:12" "Numbers 15:17–21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בקמה", :translit "bakamah", :gloss "in the standing grain"} {:he "תחל לספור", :translit "tahel lispor", :gloss "begin to count"} {:he "בקומה", :translit "bekumah", :gloss "standing (erect)"} {:he "על העומר מעומד", :translit "al ha-omer me'umad", :gloss "over the omer standing"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: בקמה (standing grain) is read as בקומה (while standing upright)"}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Dual verbal forms תספור and שבעה שבועות signal two separate counting obligations", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Reads מהחל as 'me-heil' = 'from the beginning of', linking the omer offering to the concept of ראשית", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: בקמה (standing grain) is read as בקומה (while standing upright)", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:37:01.054188910Z", :model "glm-5.2"}